        "title": "Meet Mortality Face-to-Face",
        "text": "There aren't many places in the Western world where one comes so directly face-to-face with mortality any more. Because of that, you'll either love or hate Pashupatinath. You either think the open-air funeral pires are a natural way to send loved ones back to the earth (dust to dust) or you'll find it a grotesque death ritual. Or both.\n\nPashupatinath is also more than that. It's a huge Hindu complex (although some parts are off-limits to non-Hindus). You'll see, meet, and take pictures with holy Sadus. \n\nBring a guide; you'll need one to get the most of your experience.",
