        "title": "Confronting if you witness a Cremation, but a Must See !",
        "text": "Definitely a must see, and most european visitors will be polarized by it. For myself, I was fascinated and it was a highlight, but i suspect that for some it will seem to be a shadow of what it used to be and displays something that they would consider to be distasteful. However, it must be remembered that this is a working temple for Hindu's and they are less concerned about what tourists think and more concerned about the way that they grieve their lost ones. Culturally it is as authentic as it comes and therfore for me it was perhaps one of the highlights of Nepal, along with Treking. Make sure yu get a guide, as it will make all the difference. Also don't plan to do any more temples that day as it will be hard to get your head out of this visit.",
